Mark,

  Why do you not want to use the for function? Is it because you are trying to process a vector that is 100s of thousands of elements long and it is too slow, or is it because the for function has a bad reputation? The for function is too much maligned in my opinion. It does work very well for relatively short loops.

  I am afraid that any vectorized version would require a uniform treatment of each observation--that's why it can be vectorized (by treating everything the same). If you really have a very long vector to process and need to do it many times, my suggestion would be to write a FORTRAN or C function and load the library from that.

Dave

