Eva,
  1. I am not aware of any option to identify missing values other than an
empty field or "NA"
  2. Loops using the for function are not no-nos. They can be very resource
consuming if they get to be many iterations. But the idea is to get your
work done, not to consume lots of time trying to figure out how not to use
the for function. I'd do something like this for this example:

xnam = vector of column names in x, use names(x) to generate it.
xna = vector of numeric values that represent missing values in each column
named in xnam
for(i in seq(along=xnam))
 x[[xnam[i]]] <- ifelse(x[[xnam[i]]] == xna[i], NA, x[[xnam[i]]])

  3. The sapply function seeks to simplify the result, in the example you
gave, it returns a matrix of integers, not factors, which lapply returns.
Dave

