What OS are you using? I would suggest using a vector-format image such 
as postscript or Windows metafile (wmf). Either one is accessible in 
Windows. Something along the lines of:

wmf.graph(file = "plot.wmf") # or ?postscript
plot(...)
dev.off()

Note that this prints the plot directly to a file and not to a window as 
java.graph or graphsheet would do. Also note that setting colour 
preferences is a pain in the .... This very issue is one reason I made 
the move to R years ago.

--sundar

