> A[1,3,]=c(2,5,3,7,19,87,.......)
> A[1,4,]=c(1,2,3,7,16,33,.......)
> ...............................................etc

>  I need to derive a sequence which would the intersection of all the
> "cell" sequences. In the example above it is
>  
> c(2,7,....)
>  
> Is there an intelligent way to perform this task?

tab <- table(as.vector(A))
as.numeric(names(tab[tab == p*q]))

since the sequences cannot have repeats, I understand from the examples.

