Let me encourage you to continue in the direction of storing your
S functions in files of source code.  Each file would normally contain
the source for a collection of related functions.  Modifications
would be made at the source level and then brought over to the S-Plus Commands
window.  Please see Martin Mächler's paper from the UseR! conference
for a discussion with examples.  R is a dialect of the S language, therefore
everything he says applies to S-Plus.

http://www.ci.tuwien.ac.at/Conferences/useR-2004/Keynotes/Maechler.pdf

Martin is recommending ESS with emacs as the smart editor of choice.
There are others, and he lists some.  For information about ESS,
see http://ess.r-project.org

Rich

