From garrett at NRCan.gc.ca  Tue Nov  9 13:23:17 2004
From: garrett at NRCan.gc.ca (Garrett, Robert)
Date: Tue, 09 Nov 2004 08:23:17 -0500
Subject: Summary: Lost amongst the frames, again? {[CASE#96398]}
Message-ID: <162B3F03E3AD224FA9F82DF351A15A80447975@S0-OTT-X10.NRCan.gc.ca>

The calling of multicomp following a call to aov from inside a wrapper
turned up a bug.  The problem arises in a further internal call to lm which
requires both the original data and the data frame.  The fix provided by
Insightful is in the script below and involves assigning the variable and
data frame to level (1) and then detaching them at the close of the
function.

"ja88s.aov.test" <- 
function(x, dfname, file = "d:\\s-plus\\jamaica\\")
{
        xname <- deparse(substitute(x))
        runtitle <- paste("Calling: aov(formula = ", xname, " ~ FeNaI)",
                sep = "")
        filename <- paste(file, xname, "-aov.txt", sep = "")
        aov.temp <- aov(substitute(x ~ FeNaI), dfname)
        sink(filename)
        on.exit(sink())
        cat(runtitle, "\n\n")
        print(summary(aov.temp))
        #Place the data in the default database
        assign("x", x, where = 1)
        assign("dfname", dfname, where = 1)
        print(multicomp(aov.temp))
        print(multicomp(aov.temp, method = "bon"))
        #Remove the data from default database
        remove("dfname", where = 1)
        remove("x", where = 1)
}

Thank you to Insightful staff for helping me through this.

