Hi Ahmed,

if you mean the variance-covariance matrix of the fitted multivariate 
normal distribution, then

fm <- lme(...) # your model
G <- lapply(pdMatrix(fm$modelStruct$reStruct), "*", fm$sigma^2)

gives you the fitted covariance of the random-effects. Based on this 
you can then obtain the full covariance matrix of the model V=R+ZGZ' 
by constructing Z and R, respectively.

I hope it helps.

Best,
Dimitris

