Mark,

>From ?apply:

<quote>
USAGE:
apply(X, MARGIN, FUN, ...)

OPTIONAL ARGUMENTS:

...

any arguments to FUN. They are passed unchanged to each call of FUN and 
include their names.

</quote>

So you want to do the following:

tempindex <- apply(temp, 2,
  function(x, boundthreshold) which(x == boundthreshold),
  boundthreshold = boundthreshold)

HTH,

--sundar

P.S. Do not use "_" as assignment. It is deprecated in S-PLUS 6 and will 
most likely be removed in future version of S-PLUS. In R this is already 
the case.

