On Mon, 22 Nov 2004, Rosenfeld, Simon (NIH/NCI) wrote:

> The sequences obtained by this method are not uniform and,
> more importantly, are not iid.

Given that there is a constraint on the joint distribution, the latter is 
impossible.

It is also not clear what is meant by `uniform'.  Is it marginally 
uniform, or jointly uniform over the constrained subspace?

The latter is a hard-core Strauss process in one dimension, and there are 
MCMC algorithms for it (but no exact ones AFAIK).

